#question(title: [Why the three hypotheses are necessary], centered: true)[
  You have proven

  #slide-block(title: [Theorem 3])[
    Let $a < b$. Let $f$ be a function
    defined on $[a, b]$.  \
    IF
    + $f$ is continuous on $[a, b]$
    + $f$ is differentiable on $(a, b)$
    + $f$ is not one-to-one on $[a, b]$

    THEN $display(exists c in(a comma b))$
    such that $f' (c) = 0$.
  ]

  #v(1fr)

  Give three examples to justify that each of
  the three hypotheses are necessary for the
  theorem to be true. (Graphs of the examples
  are enough).
]
